{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בקרחתו", :translit "b'karachto", :gloss "in its baldness"} {:he "אלו השחקים", :translit "elu ha'shachakim", :gloss "these are the worn-out ones"} {:he "שכשנשחק הבגד נושר השער ונעשה כמו קרח", :translit "shech'nisachak ha'beged noshar ha'se'ar v'na'aseh k'mo koreach", :gloss "for when the garment is worn out the hair falls out and it becomes like a bald spot"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical explanation: 'bald spot' (קרחת) is read as hair-loss in the garment due to wearing"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "בגבחתו", :translit "b'gabachto", :gloss "in its forelock-spot"} {:he "אלו החדשים", :translit "elu ha'chadashim", :gloss "these are the new ones"} {:he "שכשהוא חדש שערותיו בולטות", :translit "shech'shehu chadash se'arotav boltot", :gloss "for when it is new its hairs protrude"} {:he "נגע צרעת", :translit "nega tzara'at", :gloss "plague of tzara'at"} {:he "כי תזריע", :translit "ki tazri'a", :gloss "when a woman conceives (Lev 12:2 portion)"} {:he "זאת תהיה", :translit "zot tihyeh", :gloss "this shall be (Lev 14:2 portion)"} {:he "י' דברים", :translit "y' d'varim", :gloss "ten things"} {:he "נגעים באים", :translit "n'ga'im ba'im", :gloss "nega'im come"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["נגע צרעת"]} {:kind :other, :note "The two occurrences of נגע צרעת correspond to the number of sections, yielding the teaching that nega'im come through ten things"}], :frame {:text "The phrase נגע צרעת appears in Leviticus 13:2 in the portion כי תזריע and again in Leviticus 14:2 in the portion זאת תהיה. The tradition that nega'im come through ten transgressions is taught in Arakhin 16a, which lists ten things that bring nega'im.", :sources ["Leviticus 13:2" "Leviticus 14:2" "Arakhin 16a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical explanation: 'bald spot' (קרחת) is read as hair-loss in the garment due to wearing", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["נגע צרעת"], :by